          %p We now explain in more detail what this means and what it is good for.
          %h3#BasicIdea Basic idea: Monadic effects
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+language"} programming
            it frequently happens that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/program"} program
            with “nominal” output
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+type"} data type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %em de facto
            outputs data of some modified type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(D)
            which accounts for “external effects” caused by the program, where
          #eq:MonadMapInIntroduction.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D \;\mapsto\; \mathcal{E}(D)
          %p
            is some general operation sending
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to new data types
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}(D)
          %blockquote
            %p
              For example, if alongside the computation of its nominal output data
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \colon D
              a program also writes a log message
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi msg
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} msg \,\colon\,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+%28computer+science%29"} String
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi msg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d, msg)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+type"} product type
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Write
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi D
                      %mo ×
                      %mi String
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Write(D) \,\coloneqq\, D \times String
            %p
              Or, dually, if the program may fail and instead “throw an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exception"} exception
              message”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi msg
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} msg \,\colon\,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+%28computer+science%29"} String
              %em either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \colon D
              %em or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi msg
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi String
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} msg \colon String
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct+type"} coproduct type
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Excep
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
