                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            condition
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AssociativityConditionInIntroduction"} (3)
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unitality
            condition
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UnitalityInIntroduction"} (5)
            are jointly equivalent to saying that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data types
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            of
            = succeed "-effectful" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            this is known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Kl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
