                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} \circ \mathcal{E} \xrightarrow{ \mu } \mathcal{E}
              instead of the “binding” operation. One readily checks that these two axiomatic presentations of monads are in fact equal – see
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TransformBetweenBindAndJoinInIntroduction"} (7)
              below –, but the above “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+triple"}> Kleisli triple
              \/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+system"}> extension system
              ”-presentation is typically more relevant in the practice of
              = succeed "." do
