          %h3#definable_monads Definable monads
          %p
            Various monads are
            %em definable
            in terms of standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+formation"} type-forming operations
            (such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+types"} product types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Moggi91"} Moggi 1991, Exp. 1.1
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maybe+monad"} maybe monad
                encodes possible controlled failure of a program to execute.
            %li
              %p
                An
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exception+monad"} exception monad
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
                and
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreader+comonad"} coreader comonad
                both encode reading out a global parameter.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/writer+monad"} writer monad
                and
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cowriter+comonad"} cowriter comonad
                both encode writing
                %em consecutively
                into a global resource, such as for a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stream"} stream
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+monad"} state monad
                encodes the possibility of
                %em consecutive reading and re-setting
                a global parameter – this provides a notion of
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+access+memory"} random access memory
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/costate+comonad"} costate comonad
                encodes a way (a “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lens+in+computer+science"}> lens
                ”) to read and write fields in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/databases"} databases
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuation+monad"} continuation monad
                encodes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuation-passing+style"} continuation-passing style
                of program execution.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/selection+monad"} selection monad
                encodes selecting a value of a type depending on the values of some function on it.
